Day 33 – Docker Compose Basics

🚀 What I Learned

Today I started learning Docker Compose and understood how it helps manage multiple containers using a single YAML file.

Topics Covered

- What is Docker Compose?
- Why Docker Compose is used
- Difference between "docker run" and Docker Compose
- Creating "compose.yaml"
- Running containers with "docker compose up"
- Port Mapping ("80:80")

- Docker Compose commands

  - "docker compose up"
  - "docker compose down"
  - "docker compose ps"
  - "docker compose logs"
  - "docker compose start"
  - "docker compose stop"
- Volume Mounts
- Serving a custom HTML page using Nginx
- Browser testing
- Basic troubleshooting

💻 Hands-on Practice

- Created my first "compose.yaml" file.
- Deployed an Nginx container using Docker Compose.
- Added port mapping to access the website from a browser.
- Mounted a local HTML folder into the container using Docker Volumes.
- Successfully displayed my own web page through Nginx.

📚 Key Learning

Docker Compose makes it easy to manage containers using a single configuration file instead of running long Docker commands repeatedly.

